course: dictionary
lesson: 3425
title: Extinction: when a kind of living thing dies out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Extinction means that a kind of animal or plant has died out completely, so there are none left anywhere. Read the words around it for clues. «The Arabian oryx was hunted to extinction in the wild by 1972.» Hunted and «in the wild» tell you the animals were killed until none were left in nature.
explain: The word has a second meaning: something being put out or ended, such as a fire or a light. Check it in the sentence. If the meaning fits and the thing is ended for good, you have the right one.
explain: Phrases help too. «On the brink of extinction» and «facing extinction» both mean very close to dying out, so the kind is in danger but has not gone yet. «Mass extinction» means many kinds dying out at once.
fact: Extinction means a kind of animal or plant has died out completely, with none left anywhere.
fact: «Mass extinction» means many kinds dying out at once.
fact: «Steller's sea cow» was hunted to extinction in just 27 years after Europeans found it near Russia's islands in 1741.
fact: «The Arabian oryx» was hunted to extinction in the wild by 1972, but zoo-bred animals were later released in Oman.
fact: Conservation protects species from extinction, and «near extinction» means very close to dying out.
exercise: «The Arabian oryx was hunted to extinction in the wild by 1972.» What does extinction mean here? | Being put out, like a fire | A zoo where animals are kept | A long, curved horn | * When a kind of animal dies out completely, so none are left in the wild
exercise: «Island foxes were saved from near extinction.» What does near extinction mean? | Having a very big family | Very far away on an island | Being fast and clever | * Very close to dying out
exercise: Conservation protects species from extinction. What does conservation do? | Hunts species until they are gone | * Protects species from dying out | Makes new dinosaurs in a laboratory | Lets fires burn freely
test: The dodo suffered extinction. What happened to the dodo? | * Its whole kind died out and none were left | It grew into a giant animal | It learned to fly very high | It was put in a museum for children
test: «Steller's sea cow was hunted to extinction in 27 years.» Which meaning fits best? | Until it became very large | * Until none of its kind were left alive | Until it was given a new name | Until it moved to a new island
exam: What does extinction mean in «the extinction of the fire»? | A new kind of fire | * Putting out the fire, so it ends | Making a fire bigger | Lighting a fire
